Usage: agent-deck fleet recover [options]

Restart every session whose tmux session is gone but whose registry
status claims it should be running. Sessions are restarted ONE AT A
TIME with --spacing between boots, and each boot is verified before the
next one starts.

DRY RUN BY DEFAULT: without --yes the command prints the plan and exits
without restarting anything.

The sweep halts early when the failures look systemic: N consecutive
failed restarts (--max-failures), N consecutive sessions that restart and
then die immediately (--max-dead-boots), or sessions booting into an auth
failure (--auth-halt-after) — restarting the rest of the fleet against a
broken credential only deepens the cascade.

With --group-by-credential the auth halt names WHICH credential is dead
and reports one escalation per credential instead of one count for the
sweep. Opt-in: without the flag the halt message is unchanged.

Sessions the operator stopped or queued, and archived sessions, are
never touched.

Options:
  -auth-halt-after int
    	Halt after this many sessions boot into an auth failure (0 disables the auth breaker) (default 2)
  -confirm-delay duration
    	Delay between confirming probes (default 750ms)
  -confirm-probes int
    	Independent tmux probes that must agree a session is gone before it counts as down (default 2)
  -dead-fraction float
    	Share of should-be-alive sessions that must be down for a mass-death verdict (default 0.5)
  -dry-run
    	Force plan-only mode even with --yes
  -group string
    	Only consider sessions in this group path (and its descendants)
  -group-by-credential
    	Group auth-401-held sessions by which credential is dead and report one escalation per credential (opt-in, local-only; off by default the per-session view is unchanged)
  -include-idle
    	Also treat status=idle sessions as down (off by default: idle is also the status of a session that was never started)
  -jitter float
    	Random +/- fraction applied to each gap (0 disables) (default 0.2)
  -json
    	Output as JSON
  -limit int
    	Restart at most N sessions (0 = all)
  -max-dead-boots int
    	Halt after this many consecutive sessions restart and then die immediately (pane gone; 0 disables) (default 3)
  -max-failures int
    	Halt after this many consecutive failed restarts (default 3)
  -min-dead int
    	Minimum down sessions for the shape to be reported as a mass death (default 3)
  -q	Minimal output (short)
  -quiet
    	Minimal output
  -spacing duration
    	Gap between consecutive boots (0 disables spacing — not recommended) (default 5s)
  -verify-poll duration
    	Verification poll interval (default 500ms)
  -verify-timeout duration
    	How long to wait for one session to prove it booted (default 30s)
  -yes
    	Actually restart the down sessions (without this the command only prints the plan)
